WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.359
Quantization changes the approximations used during inference, so quality loss may be subtle rather than a complete failure.

00:00:08.359 --> 00:00:16.717
A response can remain fluent while becoming less precise, more repetitive, or more likely to miss a constraint.

00:00:16.717 --> 00:00:30.219
Hallucination is influenced by the base model, prompt, data, and sampling as well as precision; quantization does not create or remove it in isolation, but aggressive compression can reduce reliability.

00:00:30.219 --> 00:00:35.149
Reasoning tasks may reveal mistakes in intermediate steps or consistency.

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:41.793
Coding tasks can expose errors through compilation, tests, API use, or adherence to requirements.

00:00:41.793 --> 00:00:46.722
Instruction following should be evaluated with prompts containing several constraints.

00:00:46.722 --> 00:00:55.938
Long-context tests should check whether the model retrieves details from early and late portions rather than merely producing plausible prose.

00:00:55.938 --> 00:00:58.295
Quality sensitivity is workload-specific.

00:00:58.295 --> 00:01:07.083
A conversational assistant may tolerate a compact quantization that is unacceptable for structured extraction, technical analysis, or domain terminology.

00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:14.155
Different model architectures and quantization methods can react differently at the same nominal bit level.

00:01:14.155 --> 00:01:19.513
A strong smaller model may outperform a larger aggressively compressed model.

00:01:19.513 --> 00:01:26.586
Evaluate outputs with clear criteria: factual correctness, task completion, format compliance, consistency, and useful uncertainty.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:33.230
Use deterministic or controlled settings where possible and repeat prompts because sampling introduces variation.

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:42.874
Do not assume that a popular quant level is good enough, and do not assume every difference is caused by quantization.

00:01:42.874 --> 00:01:49.089
Compare against a higher-precision reference and the real acceptance threshold for the task.
